{"t": 1794110440.8515723, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Fixes #57.\n\n`page()` computed `start = number * size`, treating page numbers as 0-based. The API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page), so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page.\n\nChanged the offset calculation to `(number - 1) * size`.\n\nVerified locally: with `items = [1,2,3,4,5]` and `size = 2`, page 1 returns `[1,2]`, page 2 returns `[3,4]`, page 3 returns `[5]`.", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix 1-based pagination in page() (#57)"}, "ok": true}
